{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the fourth generation.</b> After they go down to Egypt they will be there three generations, and the fourth will return to this land — because it was in the land of Canaan that He spoke with him and made this covenant, as it says: ״לָתֶת לְךָ אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת לְרִשְׁתָּהּ.״ And so it was: Yaakov went down to Egypt — go count his generations: Yehudah, Peretz, and Chetzron, and Kalev ben Chetzron was among those who entered the land." "<b>For the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet complete.</b> To be driven from his land only at that time — for the Holy One, blessed be He, does not exact punishment from a nation until its measure is filled, as it says: ״בְּסַאֲסְאָהּ בְּשַׁלְּחָהּ תְּרִיבֶנָּה״ (Isaiah 27)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:50.618889658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}